WEBVTT

NOTE Captions of the how-to-play voice. This voice was made by the AI ʻohana in Shaka's voice; he blessed the lesson, the words are ours. CC BY-SA 4.0 · Open Source Orchestra

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.519
Aloha. Song one: A Planet We Share As One.

2
00:00:04.969 --> 00:00:14.373
We're in the key of G, and you only need three chords: C, G and D. The loop is C, G, D, D. Round and round, and you just sing over it.

3
00:00:14.823 --> 00:00:23.757
Keep the easy strum: one, two, three, four, all down strokes. The record sits around one twenty-nine, but today we go slower.

4
00:00:24.207 --> 00:00:33.663
The words land like this. C on Protection, G as you reach creation, then D. Must be a collaboration: C, G, D.

5
00:00:34.113 --> 00:00:41.479
Of every nation: C, G, D. For a planet we share as one: C, G, D, and land on G.

6
00:00:41.929 --> 00:00:49.557
This loop is my own; the chord placement is KALA's floor arrangement. Sing it round and round until the whole room is singing.

7
00:00:50.007 --> 00:00:56.381
This voice was made by the AI ʻohana in Shaka's voice — he blessed the lesson, the words are ours.
